<title>What's new · Dreamcore Dungeons</title>
<style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at top,#342342,#171324 65%);color:#f5eafa;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;min-height:100vh}
main{max-width:720px;margin:auto;padding:40px 22px 64px}a{color:#edbddd;text-underline-offset:4px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #edbddd;outline-offset:5px}
.eyebrow{color:#d5b9e7;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:32px}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,7vw,44px);line-height:1.15;margin:8px 0 14px}header>p:last-child{color:#cdbed9}
article{margin-top:24px;padding:24px;border:1px solid #655071;border-radius:20px;background:#241c30}h2{font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;margin:4px 0 16px}.date{color:#c8b6db;font-size:13px;margin:0}ul{padding-left:22px;margin:0}li+li{margin-top:10px}details{margin-top:20px;color:#b9a9c6;font-size:12px}summary{cursor:pointer}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}
@media(max-width:420px){main{padding:28px 16px 48px}article{padding:20px}}
</style></head><body><main><header><a href="./">← Back to the game</a>
<p class="eyebrow">Dreamcore Dungeons</p><h1>What's new?</h1>
<p>Little updates from the Dream Library. Newest first.</p></header>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-11T23:04:17.081421+00:00">11 Nov 2026 · 23:04 UTC</time></p><h2>Normal Dream, Hard and heroine progression</h2><p>Normal Dream is now the main arena route. Each heroine can keep her gear and a winning build, then take that build into Hard.</p><ul><li>Play Normal Dream through 15 arenas. Save a winning Normal build to unlock Hard for that heroine. Hard starts with the saved skills and current gear and skips XP and skill drafts.</li><li>Manage each heroine’s equipment in the Heroines menu. Compare, keep or replace her saved winning build after a Normal victory. The former dungeon run is in the Developer Tools archive.</li><li>Chill stacks can trigger Freeze and Icebreak. Cascade can hit already frozen enemies without removing Freeze, and Frostfire Orb scales with both Fire and Frost Power.</li><li>Normal shows banked levels and catches the XP display up during build breaks. After a camera drag, the view returns automatically after three seconds.</li><li>Checkpoints from earlier rules require a fresh run. Hero unlocks and remaining pulls carry forward.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261111T230417081421Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-11T16:20:56.835644+00:00">11 Nov 2026 · 16:20 UTC</time></p><h2>Dream V2 from the main hub</h2><p>The Dream Library now offers separate V1 and V2 tickets. V2 opens the full arena route with a heroine from your unlocked roster.</p><ul><li>Choose Dream V1 for the original dungeon run or Dream V2 for the full arena route directly from the hub.</li><li>Pick an unlocked heroine for a fresh V2 run, or continue from the V2 checkpoint.</li><li>Return to the hub from V2 results or retry the same arena setup. V1 and V2 keep separate checkpoints.</li><li>Checkpoints saved under earlier rules require a restart. Hero unlocks and remaining pulls stay available.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261111T162056835644Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-11T15:46:58.824843+00:00">11 Nov 2026 · 15:46 UTC</time></p><h2>Full arena route and skill priority controls</h2><p>Pacing Prototype now has a six-arena Short run and a fifteen-arena Full run. Active skills show their priority and highlight where they will land when dragged.</p><ul><li>Choose Full run in Developer Mode to fight through five dungeon tiers with a boss at the end of each tier.</li><li>Arena enemies enter in formations from the right and approach the fight from their own lane. The hero starts on the left with a fixed arena camera.</li><li>Drag active skills to change their casting priority. Numbered slots, a drag preview and a highlighted drop target show the new order.</li><li>Fixed champion drag-and-drop setup in the Archive and made empty equipment slots non-interactive.</li><li>Older run, trial and prototype checkpoints require a restart. Hero unlocks and remaining pulls stay available.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261111T154658824843Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-11T14:44:40.333943+00:00">11 Nov 2026 · 14:44 UTC</time></p><h2>Arena mini-run and skill details</h2><p>Pacing Prototype now takes place in six arenas with a centred camera. Reward cards now link to the full skill details.</p><ul><li>Fight six authored encounters with flanking waves, ranged pressure and a commander who buffs surviving enemies.</li><li>Build breaks after arenas 1, 3 and 5 advance you to levels 3, 6 and 9 and restore HP and mana.</li><li>Arena progress uses a separate save and resumes from the start of the current arena. Earlier runs, trials and prototypes require a restart. Hero unlocks and remaining pulls stay available.</li><li>Open full skill details from a reward card to see effective values and learned modifiers.</li><li>Combat sound, reduced Poolrooms effects and extra fire particle settings now persist after restarting the game.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261111T144440333943Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-11T13:56:50.440061+00:00">11 Nov 2026 · 13:56 UTC</time></p><h2>Crossbows, ranged combat and Pacing Prototype v2</h2><p>Crossbows join the ranged weapon pool, and combat targeting now uses range and valid targets without wall sight checks. Pacing Prototype v2 starts at level 1 and tests three combat sections with two build breaks.</p><ul><li>Added a slow physical crossbow family with bow range. Heavy Shot now hits a selected target, and Prism Lens adds a bounce that grows stronger along its path.</li><li>Ranged projectiles no longer pierce through enemies. Walls no longer block valid attacks, area effects or bounces within range. Walls still constrain movement.</li><li>Pacing Prototype v2 uses real class starter choices, three combat sections and two build breaks. The commander buffs surviving enemies until he falls.</li><li>Ability reward cards now flip to reveal the skill before you choose it.</li><li>Runs and trials saved under earlier rules require a restart. Hero unlocks and remaining pulls stay available.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261111T135650440061Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-10T00:39:18.660734+00:00">10 Nov 2026 · 00:39 UTC</time></p><h2>Pacing Prototype</h2><p>Developer Mode now includes a short, separately saved Pacing Prototype. It tests two combat sections, a build break and a Poolcaller fight.</p><ul><li>Open Pacing Prototype in Developer Mode and choose an On-Hit, Poison or Fire preset and a seed.</li><li>Face overlapping enemy groups with warnings before reinforcements. Between sections, choose a passive, decide whether to take an active skill, and resolve an item before continuing.</li><li>Resume at the start of the current section from a separate prototype save. Prototype runs leave normal progression alone, and the results screen can copy a test report.</li><li>Runs and trials saved under earlier rules require a restart. Hero unlocks and remaining pulls stay available.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261110T003918660734Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-09T23:49:12.424512+00:00">09 Nov 2026 · 23:49 UTC</time></p><h2>Hero unlocks and Champion Trial results</h2><p>Hero unlocks and remaining pulls survive restarting after an incompatible saved run or trial. This build also includes the Champion Trial results fix.</p><ul><li>Preserved unlocked heroines and remaining pulls when restarting after an incompatible saved run or trial. The original save stays backed up.</li><li>Fixed recursive results navigation when a timed Champion Trial ends.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261109T234912424512Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-09T23:08:44.938167+00:00">09 Nov 2026 · 23:08 UTC</time></p><h2>Cached startup, combat readability and playtest privacy</h2><p>The start screen now offers Play when the current build is cached. This update also improves combat readability, simplifies peaceful encounters and updates voluntary playtest sharing.</p><ul><li>Play appears when both game files are cached; the download prompt estimates only the files still needed.</li><li>Added compact skill details, hold-to-inspect controls and clearer combat numbers on phones. Level-up effects now appear on the reward cards.</li><li>Peaceful encounters use shorter approach and exit paths; active skills are disabled outside combat. Navigation skips detailed searches between disconnected areas.</li><li>Fixed a crash when opening the result after a timed Champion Trial.</li><li>Playtest sharing requires a fresh opt-in with 18+ confirmation. Withdrawing consent stops uploads and requests deletion of shared data, with retry when back online.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261109T230844938167Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-06T14:42:43.658746+00:00">06 Nov 2026 · 14:42 UTC</time></p><h2>Solo runs, Blacksmith and combat performance</h2><p>Normal runs are now solo, with a Blacksmith visit at the start of Dungeon 4. This update also changes crafting access, reduces repeated combat work and refreshes menu and dungeon visuals.</p><ul><li>Reduced repeated combat work with shared actor lookups, budgeted path searches and cached runtime stats.</li><li>Removed mercenary recruitment from normal runs. The Blacksmith at the start of Dungeon 4 lets you choose one equipped item, craft it with your materials, then finish or skip the visit.</li><li>Craft unresolved drops before equipping them. Accepted and merchant gear stays sealed outside the Blacksmith session; replacement comparisons no longer reveal randomized salvage materials.</li><li>Character, damage and settings popups now share glass panels, compact value tables and sizing based on their contents. Removed the duplicate portrait from the settings popup.</li><li>Added themed entrances and open/closed exits for the poolrooms, suburb, mall and windmill dungeons.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261106T144243658746Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-06T13:36:33.251631+00:00">06 Nov 2026 · 13:36 UTC</time></p><h2>Download prompt and rendering fixes</h2><p>The loading screen now asks before downloading the game and shows its size and progress in MB. Small effect and reward polygons also render more reliably.</p><ul><li>Added a download confirmation with the game-file size, Download &amp; play and Not now. The large engine and game files start downloading only after confirmation; loading progress shows loaded and total MB.</li><li>Postponing the download or closing during loading remains a session diagnostic rather than a bug report. Genuine download, startup, JavaScript and engine errors remain reportable.</li><li>Fixed polygon triangulation errors in shrinking combat fragments and shared ticket/reward surfaces while preserving their visible shapes.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261106T133633251631Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-05T14:06:52.191084+00:00">05 Nov 2026 · 14:06 UTC</time></p><h2>Playtest upload improvements</h2><p>Playtest uploads now respect service retry times and keep daily-limit pauses after reloading. Recording and uploads read less local history.</p><ul><li>Playtest uploads honor server retry delays. Daily-limit pauses persist across page reloads and reconnects while pending records remain queued within the existing storage limit.</li><li>Reduced local history reads during playtest recording and uploads. Existing acknowledged history remains available for local export.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261105T140652191084Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-04T21:43:21.945322+00:00">04 Nov 2026 · 21:43 UTC</time></p><h2>Equipment and loot rework</h2><p>Loot now equips directly or becomes crafting materials. Replacing equipment automatically salvages the previous item, and equipped gear can be crafted between fights.</p><ul><li>Removed the backpack and backup item slots. Only equipped gear is retained; each pending loot item must be equipped or salvaged before continuing.</li><li>Equipping loot or accepting the free merchant item replaces the same-slot item and salvages it once. Comparisons show the replacement material and skills incompatible with the new weapon.</li><li>Replaced inventory swapping with a four-slot equipment screen. Crafting works on equipped hero gear outside combat and on pending loot; companion equipment remains fixed.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261104T214321945322Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-04T15:11:07.051426+00:00">04 Nov 2026 · 15:11 UTC</time></p><h2>Combat and build rework</h2><p>Reworked weapon combat, class starts and build upgrades, with weapon drops that better reflect your build. Navigation now does less repeated work in crowded fights.</p><ul><li>Added class-specific starter choices with a core skill and matching weapon. Weapon enhancers now combine on the original autoattack in configured order, with shared action-level mana budgets.</li><li>Raised Heavy Strike to 1,000% attack and added Focused Discharge (+60% direct Lightning Strike damage). Reverberation offers now consider effective lightning sources, including Storm Cabinet, while remaining available without one.</li><li>Weapon drops and merchants now roll a weapon family before a specific weapon. Matching skills provide the main weighting bonus, capped at 2x; other weapon families remain available.</li><li>Skill maps now distinguish prerequisites, upgrades, synergies, alternatives and exclusions. Added 24 build-direction presets; compatible upgrades can be combined instead of treated as exclusive forms.</li><li>Reduced repeated collision and pathfinding work in crowded fights. Blocked actors wait briefly before retrying instead of continuously searching for another attack position. Added a persistent 60/120 FPS setting, with 120 FPS as the default.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261104T151107051426Z</code></details></article>
<article><p class="date"><time datetime="2026-11-04T13:03:59.766724+00:00">04 Nov 2026 · 13:03 UTC</time></p><h2>Dream Ticket fix :3</h2><p>Fixed a Dream Ticket rendering error. This update also simplifies playtest consent and reduces upload data.</p><ul><li>Fixed a polygon triangulation error in the Dream Ticket shimmer when returning from the hero gallery to the start screen.</li><li>Replaced the initial playtest consent screen with a compact dialog and expandable data details.</li><li>Reduced playtest upload size with compressed batches and smaller build snapshots.</li></ul><details><summary>Build details</summary><code>20261104T130359766724Z</code></details></article></main><script>
for (const time of document.querySelectorAll('time[datetime]')) {
 time.textContent = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {timeZone:'Europe/Vienna',dateStyle:'medium',timeStyle:'short'}).format(new Date(time.dateTime));
}
</script></body></html>
